# RegDelta — ownership boundaries. See docs/governance/ROLES.md.
#
# NOT mechanically enforced. This repo has a single human, so a required
# code-owner review is unsatisfiable — the author cannot approve their own
# PR, and every @regdelta-* placeholder resolved to nothing (all five 404'd,
# and team syntax needs an org this repo does not have). The file enforced
# exactly zero of the boundaries it appeared to. See ADR-0005.
#
# The seat names below are therefore a routing map, not a gate: they say
# which role subagent must review a path (.claude/agents/) and which
# checklist item in the PR template carries the attestation. The real
# enforcement is the agent pass plus the eval gate — which is what actually
# caught M01's merge-blocking HIGH.
#
# Owner mapped to the one account that can hold it. Re-split the seats if
# this repo ever moves to an org with real teams.

# Product owns WHAT to build and when it's acceptable
/SPEC/                          @andaro74
/milestones/                    @andaro74

# The SME owns what CORRECT means. Engineering may never self-approve
# changes to ground truth — this is the core AI-accountability boundary.
# /evals/ is eng+SME co-owned (SPEC/02 prerequisite C, M00b finding 5):
# without it, retrieval_truth.json and run_evals.py — the code that decides
# whether ground truth was met — would have no owner at all. Last match
# wins, so the golden-set line below stays SME-only.
/evals/                         @andaro74
/evals/golden_questions.json    @andaro74
# The demo's questions are product SCOPE, not SME truth and not an engineering
# probe set: they assert what the demo asks and who it claims to be asking as
# (company_profile). Changing a scenario's question changes what the milestone
# demonstrates, so it wants the same stop-and-decide treatment as ground truth.
# Placed after the golden-set line because last match wins.
/evals/scenarios.json           @andaro74
# The admitted-false-fail register (SPEC/07 item 5, ADR-0015). Each entry is an
# SME-seat ruling that one recorded answer's failure is a false fail, and an
# entry suppresses a failure in `unit` — the check that gates merge. So it is
# SME-owned for the same reason ground truth is, and placed after the lines
# above because last match wins.
#
# THIS LINE IS THE FIX FOR A REAL HOLE, not a formality. security-reviewer
# (M07 M2) observed that one PR can add both an entry AND the ruling document
# it cites, so the entry becomes usable in the commit that introduces it and
# the falsifiability control has no mechanical backing. `cites_ruling` cannot
# close that — it can only ask whether the document is in the tree, and in
# that PR it is. A code-owner review requirement on this path can, because the
# seat that must approve is not the seat that wrote it.
#
# It is NOT closed today: with `require_code_owner_review: false` and one
# collaborator, this file enforces nothing (ADR-0005). It closes when Door 1
# lands. Recorded in ADR-0015 as an open hole rather than claimed as a fix.
/evals/admitted_false_fails.json @andaro74
